# Technical Design Documents

This directory contains Technical Design Documents (TDDs) for {{PROJECT_NAME}}.

## What is a TDD?

A TDD describes the technical approach for implementing a complex feature or system component.

## When to Create a TDD

Create a TDD when:
- Implementing a complex feature
- Making significant changes to existing systems
- The approach isn't obvious
- Multiple components need coordination

## Template

```markdown
# Design: Feature Name

## Overview
Brief description of what this design covers.

## Goals
- What we're trying to achieve

## Non-Goals
- What this design explicitly doesn't cover

## Background
Context needed to understand this design.

## Detailed Design
### Component 1
How it works...

### Component 2
How it works...

## Alternatives Considered
Other approaches and why they weren't chosen.

## Security Considerations
Any security implications.

## Testing Strategy
How this will be tested.

## Rollout Plan
How this will be deployed.
```

